{"results":[{"id":"6acf8533a44062761084826c","name":"Ivanti CVE-2026-104935: Zero-Day Chain Exploited in Operation Innovate","description":"Ivanti has released emergency security updates after attackers exploited a chain of three zero-day vulnerabilities in Connect Secure VPN appliances to gain root-level access without authentication. The attack began on October 3, targeting an appliance running version 22.8R2.4. Two vulnerabilities are tracked as CVE-2026-104935 with a CVSS score of 8.6, involving an authentication bypass and remote code execution through manipulated CGI requests and malicious file uploads. A third unpatched vulnerability allows privilege escalation to root by manipulating a privileged service through memory modification. While patches address the authentication bypass and RCE, the privilege escalation flaw remains unresolved. CISA added the vulnerability to its KEV catalog with an October 16 remediation deadline for federal agencies.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-13T13:01:58.949000","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:47.783000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4526679583,"indicator":"CVE-2026-104935","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["vpn appliances","ivanti connect secure","root access","race condition","cgi exploitation","privilege escalation","authentication bypass","cve-2026-104935","zero-day vulnerabilities"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1557","T1548.003","T1069","T1003.004","T1087.002","T1190","T1558","T1070.001","T1550.003","T1110","T1078","T1068","T1203","T1070.004","T1105","T1211"],"references":["https:\/\/op-c.net\/blog\/ivanti-cve-2026-104935-zero-day-rce-exploit\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6acf85338bff164de62a2759","name":"Hirudo: From Fake Updates to Patched Banking Apps","description":"A new Android banking remote access trojan named Hirudo has been identified, combining credential theft with live remote control. It is delivered through shopping and entertainment apps that act as droppers, installing the trojan as a separate package behind fake update prompts. The malware replaces legitimate banking applications with patched versions that disable security checks from within the app itself. Eight Indonesian banking apps covering seven banks have been targeted with purpose-built replacements embedding a hooking engine. The campaign uses real advertising infrastructure including Amazon CloudFront for distribution, with targeting extending beyond Indonesia to China, India, Mexico, Morocco, Thailand, and Malaysia. Backend data from August 2026 revealed thousands of stolen credentials and device records.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-13T13:01:58.949000","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:47.216000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4527203187,"indicator":"3ccd2c02cf0661613816ca30032b4cdd","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203188,"indicator":"3b14859a3a1219515f89ff453c7031f3dc8a95d7","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203189,"indicator":"0097a0406be20544e98e981075427f40789db40fe4a53b1b4523383a945328b7","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203190,"indicator":"2e45277acfde3fb704179476b08f428f66a03670bbdbf2e8ec79c0b0333c009b","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203191,"indicator":"425cd7072b5e9386ac94e97fe272980b6ef36240df6b5d77b371ab7378004c83","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203192,"indicator":"b2270c29b3d0a49a716730d6ef108cffec0b1a4b159dd02e93333fb85e492b99","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203193,"indicator":"d51f2bd7ffb49c224d8eaec2c8ca1c8ab9fce2fd5fdceea01eb54296c2f47b4d","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203194,"indicator":"f796eb9ecf516e4f1fafcf89200d9f7d8ddd234f705e63f1bc8fc3ef583f0248","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203199,"indicator":"http:\/\/43.225.157.157:8766\/request_token","type":"URL","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203200,"indicator":"jiekou.baojingtextile.cn","type":"hostname","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4527203201,"indicator":"www.helloharmonyos.com","type":"hostname","created":"2026-10-14T13:35:48","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["device takeover","indonesia targeting","android banking trojan","app patching","hirudo","rat","fake updates","credential theft"],"targeted_countries":["British Indian Ocean Territory","China","India","Indonesia","Malaysia","Mexico","Morocco","Thailand"],"malware_families":["Hirudo"],"attack_ids":["T1056"],"references":["https:\/\/www.threatfabric.com\/blogs\/hirudo-from-fake-updates-to-patched-banking-apps"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6acf7922d9bc17d95d27ec5c","name":"ClingSTUN Turns Vulnerable Edge Devices Into Attacker Infrastructure","description":"An evolving Linux malware campaign deploys ClingSTUN, a back-connect proxy backdoor exploiting known vulnerabilities in Internet-facing IoT and network devices. The malware establishes persistent access and converts compromised systems into remotely controlled proxy nodes. Supporting multiple Linux architectures, ClingSTUN combines boot persistence, process termination, watchdog manipulation, process concealment, remote command execution, and self-propagation. It abuses legitimate public STUN infrastructure for NAT traversal. The campaign has expanded the number of vulnerabilities and device vendors it targets over time, affecting products from D-Link, EnGenius, Realtek, TP-Link, AVTECH, Ivanti, Tenda, Lantronix, and others, highlighting the continued risk posed by unpatched, unsupported, and unnecessarily exposed Internet-facing devices.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-13T12:01:20.995000","created":"2026-10-14T12:44:18.127000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":2199241492,"indicator":"CVE-2017-7921","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-14T12:44:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":2873968331,"indicator":"CVE-2021-21974","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-14T12:44:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":2959959659,"indicator":"CVE-2021-3493","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-14T12:44:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":3355305903,"indicator":"CVE-2022-21894","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-14T12:44:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":3363701643,"indicator":"CVE-2021-4034","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-14T12:44:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":3463951560,"indicator":"CVE-2022-30190","typ