https:\/\/asec.ahnlab.com\/ko\/96512\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6af6c512eff4af48c4b11a6b","name":"European Refrigeration Systems Cyber Sabotage","description":"A series of cyberattacks targeting commercial refrigeration infrastructure across Europe exposed critical vulnerabilities in operational technology systems. Beginning October 2026 in France with approximately 700 affected supermarkets, the campaign expanded in November to Belgium, Luxembourg, Sweden, Netherlands, Ireland, Estonia, Portugal, Italy, Finland, Germany, and Romania. Attackers manipulated refrigeration management interfaces, altering defrost cycles and temperature settings, causing product losses and business disruptions. France attributed the October attacks to Iran's IRGC unit Shahid Kaveh, while Russian-aligned groups NoName057(16) and Z-Pentest claimed responsibility for the broader campaign. Technical analysis reveals the attacks exploited default configurations, weak passwords, and internet-exposed management systems rather than sophisticated malware. The incidents affected food retailers and attempted intrusions against meat-processing facilities and medical cold-storage systems, demonstr...","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-13T09:23:21.421000","created":"2026-11-13T08:06:42.451000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Cyber Av3ngers","indicators":[{"id":4524829354,"indicator":"CVE-2025-41450","type":"CVE","created":"2026-11-13T08:06:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4524829355,"indicator":"CVE-2025-41451","type":"CVE","created":"2026-11-13T08:06:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4525409005,"indicator":"CVE-2025-41452","type":"CVE","created":"2026-11-13T08:06:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4565093543,"indicator":"188.208.141.210","typ